@startuml Fat Handler Anti-Pattern
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

title **HIGH: Fat Handler Anti-Pattern - StripeRefundRequestHandler**

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor<<expected>> #C8E6C9
    BorderColor<<expected>> #43A047
    BackgroundColor<<actual>> #FFCDD2
    BorderColor<<actual>> #E53935
}

rectangle "Expected: Thin Handler (15-25 lines)" <<expected>> {
    rectangle "RefundRequestHandler" as thin {
        rectangle "handle(event)" as thin_handle
    }
    rectangle "RefundService" as svc {
        rectangle "processRefund()" as svc_method
    }
    thin_handle --> svc_method : delegate
}

rectangle "Actual: Fat Handler (~250 lines)" <<actual>> {
    rectangle "StripeRefundRequestHandler" as fat {
        rectangle "handle()" as fat1
        rectangle "loadOrder()" as fat2
        rectangle "getPaymentIntentId()" as fat3
        rectangle "getChargeId()" as fat4
        rectangle "buildRefundParams()" as fat5
        rectangle "executeStripeRefund()" as fat6
        rectangle "updateOrderAfterRefund()" as fat7
        rectangle "logRefundRequest()" as fat8
    }
}

fat1 --> fat2 : Line 64
fat2 --> fat3 : Line 70
fat3 --> fat4 : Line 76
fat4 --> fat5 : Line 82
fat5 --> fat6 : Line 85
fat6 --> fat7 : Line 91
fat7 --> fat8 : Line 94

note right of fat
    **7 Responsibilities in 1 Handler**
    Violates Single Responsibility Principle

    Target: 15-25 lines
    Actual: ~250 lines
end note

note bottom
    **Should be extracted to:**
    - RefundService (business logic)
    - StripeRefundAdapter (API calls)
    - RefundLogger (logging)
end note

@enduml
